# Line endings for the file types this repository's tooling actually reads.
#
# Scoped on purpose. A blanket `* text=auto` would renormalize files that are
# already stored with mixed or binary-detected content
# (backend/src/utils/studentImportClassifier.js is stored mixed,
# backend/tests/driverDocuments.unit.test.js is stored as -text), turning an
# unrelated whole-file rewrite into part of every future diff.
#
# Shell scripts are the reason this file exists: production-readiness-gate.sh,
# restore-drill-db.sh and the backup scripts are executed by /bin/sh on the
# server, where a CR at the end of a shebang or a `then` is a syntax error.
# JS, JSON and Markdown follow so evidence bundles, manifests and closure
# reports hash the same way on every machine that regenerates them.

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

scripts/*.js         text eol=lf
scripts/**/*.js      text eol=lf
backend/scripts/*.js text eol=lf
backend/tests/*.js   text eol=lf

# Already stored as binary-detected content; leave it exactly as git has it
# rather than renormalizing a file this work never touched.
backend/tests/driverDocuments.unit.test.js -text
